                                  'Deafened, Exhaustion, Frightened, Grappled, Prone,\n'
                                  'Restrained\n'
                                  'Senses Blindsight 60 ft.; Passive Perception 8\n'
                                  'Languages None\n'
                                  'CR 4 (XP 1,100; PB +2)\n'
                                  'Traits\n'
                                  'Amorphous. The pudding can move through a space\n'
                                  'as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra move-\n'
                                  'ment to do so.\n'
                                  'Corrosive Form. A creature that hits the pudding with a\n'
                                  'melee attack roll takes 4 (1d8) Acid damage. Nonmag-\n'
                                  'ical ammunition is destroyed immediately after hitting\n'
                                  'the pudding and dealing any damage. Any nonmagical\n'
                                  'weapon takes a cumulative −1 penalty to attack rolls\n'
                                  'immediately after dealing damage to the pudding and\n'
                                  'coming into contact with it. The weapon is destroyed if\n'
                                  'the penalty reaches −5. The penalty can be removed by\n'
                                  'casting the Mending spell on the weapon.\n'
                                  'In 1 minute, the pudding can eat through 2 feet of\n'
                                  'nonmagical wood or metal.\n'
                                  'Spider Climb. The pudding can climb difficult surfaces,\n'
                                  'including along ceilings, without needing to make an\n'
                                  'ability check.\n'
                                  'Actions\n'
                                  'Dissolving Pseudopod. Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach\n'
                                  '10 ft. Hit: 17 (4d6 + 3) Acid damage. Nonmagical ar-\n'
                                  'mor worn by the target takes a −1 penalty to the AC it\n'
                                  'offers. The armor is destroyed if the penalty reduces its\n'
                                  'AC to 10. The penalty can be removed by casting the\n'
                                  'Mending spell on the armor.\n'
                                  'Reactions\n'
                                  'Split. Trigger: While the pudding is Large or Medium\n'
                                  'and has 10+ Hit Points, it becomes Bloodied or is sub-\n'
                                  'jected to Lightning or Slashing damage. Response: The\n'
                                  'pudding splits into two new Black Puddings. Each new\n'
                                  'pudding is one size smaller than the original pudding\n'
                                  'and acts on its Initiative. The original pudding’s Hit\n'
                                  '\n'
                                  'Points are divided evenly between the new puddings\n'
                                  '(round down).\n'
