                                    'Senses Darkvision 60 ft., Tremorsense 60 ft.;\n'
                                    'Passive Perception 10\n'
                                    'Languages Primordial (Terran)\n'
                                    'CR 5 (XP 1,800; PB +3)\n'
                                    'Traits\n'
                                    'Earth Glide. The elemental can burrow through\n'
                                    'nonmagical, unworked earth and stone. While do-\n'
                                    'ing so, the elemental doesn’t disturb the material it\n'
                                    'moves through.\n'
                                    'Siege Monster. The elemental deals double damage to\n'
                                    'objects and structures.\n'
                                    'Actions\n'
                                    'Multiattack. The elemental makes two attacks, using\n'
                                    'Slam or Rock Launch in any combination.\n'
                                    'Slam. Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8\n'
                                    '+ 5) Bludgeoning damage.\n'
                                    '\n'
                                    'Rock Launch. Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit:\n'
                                    '8 (1d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large\n'
                                    'or smaller creature, it has the Prone condition.\n'
                                    'Efreeti\n'
                                    'Efreeti\n'
                                    'Large Elemental (Genie), Neutral\n'
                                    'AC 17\t\t Initiative +1 (11)\n'
                                    'HP 212 (17d10 + 119)\n'
                                    'Speed 40 ft., Fly 60 ft. (hover)\n'
                                    'MOD SAVE MOD SAVE MOD SAVE\n'
                                    'Str 22 +6 +6 Dex 12 +1 +1 Con 24 +7 +7\n'
                                    'Int 16 +3 +3 Wis 15 +2 +6 Cha 19 +4 +8\n'
                                    'Immunities Fire\n'
                                    'Senses Darkvision 120 ft.; Passive Perception 12\n'
                                    'Languages Primordial (Ignan)\n'
                                    'CR 11 (XP 7,200; PB +4)\n'
                                    'Traits\n'
                                    'Elemental Restoration. If the efreeti dies outside the\n'
                                    'Elemental Plane of Fire, its body dissolves into ash, and\n'
                                    'it gains a new body in 1d4 days, reviving with all its Hit\n'
                                    'Points somewhere on the Plane of Fire.\n'
                                    'Magic Resistance. The efreeti has Advantage on saving\n'
                                    'throws against spells and other magical effects.\n'
                                    'Wishes. The efreeti has a 30 percent chance of know-\n'
                                    'ing the Wish spell. If the efreeti knows it, the efreeti\n'
                                    'can cast it only on behalf of a non-genie creature who\n'
                                    'communicates a wish in a way the efreeti can under-\n'
                                    'stand. If the efreeti casts the spell for the creature, the\n'
                                    'efreeti suffers none of the spell’s stress. Once the efreeti\n'
                                    'has cast it three times, the efreeti can’t do so again\n'
                                    'for 365 days.\n'
                                    'Actions\n'
                                    'Multiattack. The efreeti makes three attacks, using\n'
                                    'Heated Blade or Hurl Flame in any combination.\n'
                                    'Heated Blade. Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft.\n'
                                    'Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Slashing damage plus 13 (2d12)\n'
                                    'Fire damage.\n'
                                    'Hurl Flame. Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 120 ft. Hit:\n'
                                    '24 (7d6) Fire damage.\n'
                                    'Spellcasting. The efreeti casts one of the following\n'
                                    'spells, requiring no Material components and using\n'
                                    'Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 16):\n'
                                    'At Will: Detect Magic, Elementalism\n'
                                    '1/Day Each: Gaseous Form, Invisibility, Major Image,\n'
                                    'Plane Shift, Tongues, Wall of Fire (level 7 version)\n'
                                    'Erinyes\n'
                                    'Erinyes\n'
                                    'Medium Fiend (Devil), Lawful Evil\n'
                                    'AC 18\t\t Initiative +7 (17)\n'
                                    'HP 178 (21d8 + 84)\n'
                                    'Speed 30 ft., Fly 60 ft.\n'
                                    'MOD SAVE MOD SAVE MOD SAVE\n'
                                    'Str 18 +4 +4 Dex 16 +3 +7 Con 18 +4 +8\n'
                                    'Int 14 +2 +2 Wis 14 +2 +2 Cha 18 +4 +8\n'
                                    'Skills Perception +6, Persuasion +8\n'
                                    'Resistances Cold\n'
                                    'Immunities Fire, Poison; Poisoned\n'
                                    'Senses Truesight 120 ft.; Passive Perception 16\n'
                                    'Languages Infernal; telepathy 120 ft.\n'
                                    'CR 12 (XP 8,400; PB +4)\n'
                                    'Traits\n'
                                    'Diabolical Restoration. If the erinyes dies outside the\n'
                                    'Nine Hells, its body disappears in sulfurous smoke, and\n'
                                    'it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its Hit\n'
                                    'Points somewhere in the Nine Hells.\n'
                                    'Magic Resistance. The erinyes has Advantage on saving\n'
                                    'throws against spells and other magical effects.\n'
                                    'Magic Rope. The erinyes has a magic rope. While bear-\n'
                                    'ing it, the erinyes can use the Entangling Rope action.\n'
                                    'The rope has AC 20, HP 90, and Immunity to Poison\n'
                                    'and Psychic damage. The rope turns to dust if reduced\n'
                                    'to 0 Hit Points, if it is 5+ feet away from the erinyes\n'
                                    'for 1 hour or more, or if the erinyes dies. If the rope is\n'
                                    'damaged or destroyed, the erinyes can fully restore it\n'
                                    'when finishing a Short or Long Rest.\n'
                                    'Actions\n'
                                    'Multiattack. The erinyes makes three Withering Sword\n'
                                    'attacks and can use Entangling Rope.\n'
                                    'Withering Sword. Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft.\n'
                                    'Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 11 (2d10) Ne-\n'
                                    'crotic damage.\n'
                                    'Entangling Rope (Requires Magic Rope). Strength\n'
                                    'Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature the erinyes can see\n'
                                    'within 120 feet. Failure: 14 (4d6) Force damage, and the\n'
                                    'target has the Restrained condition until the rope is de-\n'
                                    'stroyed, the erinyes uses a Bonus Action to release the\n'
                                    'target, or the erinyes uses Entangling Rope again.\n'
                                    'Reactions\n'
                                    'Parry. Trigger: The erinyes is hit by a melee attack roll\n'
                                    'while holding a weapon. Response: The erinyes adds 4\n'
                                    'to its AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss.\n'
                                    '\n'
