                                      'Traits\n'
                                      'Aberrant Ground. The ground in a 10-foot Emanation\n'
                                      'originating from the mouther is Difficult Terrain.\n'
                                      'Gibbering. The mouther babbles incoherently while\n'
                                      'it doesn’t have the Incapacitated condition. Wisdom\n'
                                      'Saving Throw: DC 10, any creature that starts its turn\n'
                                      'within 20 feet of the mouther while it is babbling.\n'
                                      'Failure: The target rolls 1d8 to determine what it does\n'
                                      'during the current turn:\n'
                                      '1–4. The target does nothing.\n'
                                      '5–6. The target takes no action or Bonus Action and\n'
                                      'uses all its movement to move in a random direction.\n'
                                      '7–8. The target makes a melee attack against a ran-\n'
                                      'domly determined creature within its reach or does\n'
                                      'nothing if it can’t make such an attack.\n'
                                      'Actions\n'
                                      'Bite. Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6)\n'
                                      'Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller\n'
                                      'creature, it has the Prone condition. The target dies if\n'
                                      'it is reduced to 0 Hit Points by this attack. Its body is\n'
                                      'then absorbed into the mouther, leaving only equip-\n'
                                      'ment behind.\n'
                                      'Blinding Spittle (Recharge 5–6). Dexterity Saving\n'
                                      'Throw: DC 10, each creature in a 10-foot-radius Sphere\n'
                                      'centered on a point within 30 feet. Failure: 7 (2d6) Ra-\n'
                                      'diant damage, and the target has the Blinded condition\n'
                                      'until the end of the mouther’s next turn.\n'
                                      '\n'
