                              'Int 1 −5 −5 Wis 6 −2 −2 Cha 2 −4 −4\n'
                              'Skills Stealth +2\n'
                              'Resistances Acid, Cold, Fire\n'
                              'Immunities Blinded, Charmed, Deafened, Exhaustion,\n'
                              'Frightened, Grappled, Prone, Restrained\n'
                              'Senses Blindsight 60 ft.; Passive Perception 8\n'
                              'Languages None\n'
                              'CR 1/2 (XP 100; PB +2)\n'
                              'Traits\n'
                              'Amorphous. The ooze can move through a space\n'
                              'as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra move-\n'
                              'ment to do so.\n'
                              'Corrosive Form. Nonmagical ammunition is destroyed\n'
                              'immediately after hitting the ooze and dealing any\n'
                              'damage. Any nonmagical weapon takes a cumulative\n'
                              '−1 penalty to attack rolls immediately after dealing\n'
                              'damage to the ooze and coming into contact with it.\n'
                              'The weapon is destroyed if the penalty reaches −5. The\n'
                              'penalty can be removed by casting the Mending spell\n'
                              'on the weapon.\n'
                              'The ooze can eat through 2-inch-thick, nonmagical\n'
                              'metal or wood in 1 round.\n'
                              'Actions\n'
                              'Pseudopod. Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10\n'
                              '(2d8 + 1) Acid damage. Nonmagical armor worn by the\n'
                              'target takes a −1 penalty to the AC it offers. The armor\n'
                              'is destroyed if the penalty reduces its AC to 10. The\n'
                              'penalty can be removed by casting the Mending spell\n'
                              'on the armor.\n'
