                          'Skills Arcana +19, History +12, Insight +9, Perception +9\n'
                          'Resistances Cold, Lightning\n'
                          'Immunities Necrotic, Poison; Charmed, Exhaustion,\n'
                          'Frightened, Paralyzed, Poisoned\n'
                          'Gear Component Pouch\n'
                          'Senses Truesight 120 ft.; Passive Perception 19\n'
                          'Languages All\n'
                          'CR 21 (XP 33,000, or 41,000 in lair; PB +7)\n'
                          'Traits\n'
                          'Legendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair). If\n'
                          'the lich fails a saving throw, it can choose to suc-\n'
                          'ceed instead.\n'
                          'Spirit Jar. If destroyed, the lich reforms in 1d10 days\n'
                          'if it has a spirit jar, reviving with all its Hit Points. The\n'
                          'new body appears in an unoccupied space within the\n'
                          'lich’s lair.\n'
                          'Actions\n'
                          'Multiattack. The lich makes three attacks, using El-\n'
                          'dritch Burst or Paralyzing Touch in any combination.\n'
                          'Eldritch Burst. Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +12, reach\n'
                          '5 ft. or range 120 ft. Hit: 31 (4d12 + 5) Force damage.\n'
                          'Paralyzing Touch. Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 5\n'
                          'ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Cold damage, and the target has\n'
                          'the Paralyzed condition until the start of the lich’s\n'
                          'next turn.\n'
                          'Spellcasting. The lich casts one of the following spells,\n'
                          'using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (spell\n'
                          'save DC 20):\n'
                          'At Will: Detect Magic, Detect Thoughts, Dispel Magic,\n'
                          'Fireball (level 5 version), Invisibility, Lightning Bolt\n'
                          '(level 5 version), Mage Hand, Prestidigitation\n'
                          '2/Day Each: Animate Dead, Dimension Door,\n'
                          'Plane Shift\n'
                          '1/Day Each: Chain Lightning, Finger of Death, Power\n'
                          'Word Kill, Scrying\n'
                          'Reactions\n'
                          'Protective Magic. The lich casts Counterspell or Shield\n'
                          'in response to the spell’s trigger, using the same spell-\n'
                          'casting ability as Spellcasting.\n'
                          'Legendary Actions\n'
                          'Legendary Action Uses: 3 (4 in Lair). Immediately after\n'
                          'another creature’s turn, the lich can expend a use to take\n'
                          'one of the following actions. The lich regains all expended\n'
                          'uses at the start of each of its turns.\n'
                          'Deathly Teleport. The lich teleports up to 60 feet to\n'
                          'an unoccupied space it can see, and each creature\n'
                          'within 10 feet of the space it left takes 11 (2d10) Ne-\n'
                          'crotic damage.\n'
                          'Disrupt Life. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 20, each\n'
                          'creature that isn’t an Undead in a 20-foot Emanation\n'
                          'originating from the lich. Failure: 31 (9d6) Necrotic\n'
                          'damage. Success: Half damage. Failure or Success:\n'
                          'The lich can’t take this action again until the start of its\n'
                          'next turn.\n'
                          'Frightening Gaze. The lich casts Fear, using the same\n'
                          'spellcasting ability as Spellcasting. The lich can’t take\n'
                          'this action again until the start of its next turn.\n'
