                                      'instantly, reviving with all its Hit Points somewhere in\n'
                                      'Mount Celestia.\n'
                                      'Legendary Resistance (4/Day). If the solar fails a saving\n'
                                      'throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n'
                                      'Magic Resistance. The solar has Advantage on saving\n'
                                      'throws against spells and other magical effects.\n'
                                      'Actions\n'
                                      'Multiattack. The solar makes two Flying Sword attacks.\n'
                                      'It can replace one attack with a use of Slaying Bow.\n'
                                      'Flying Sword. Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +15, reach\n'
                                      '10 ft. or range 120 ft. Hit: 22 (4d6 + 8) Slashing damage\n'
                                      'plus 36 (8d8) Radiant damage. Hit or Miss: The sword\n'
                                      'magically returns to the solar’s hand or hovers within 5\n'
                                      'feet of the solar immediately after a ranged attack.\n'
                                      'Slaying Bow. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 21, one crea-\n'
                                      'ture the solar can see within 600 feet. Failure: If the\n'
                                      'creature has 100 Hit Points or fewer, it dies. It other-\n'
                                      'wise takes 24 (4d8 + 6) Piercing damage plus 36 (8d8)\n'
                                      'Radiant damage.\n'
                                      'Spellcasting. The solar casts one of the following spells,\n'
                                      'requiring no Material components and using Charisma\n'
                                      'as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 25):\n'
                                      'At Will: Detect Evil and Good\n'
                                      '1/Day Each: Commune, Control Weather, Dispel Evil\n'
                                      'and Good, Resurrection\n'
                                      'Bonus Actions\n'
                                      'Divine Aid (3/Day). The solar casts Cure Wounds (level\n'
                                      '2 version), Lesser Restoration, or Remove Curse, using\n'
                                      'the same spellcasting ability as Spellcasting.\n'
                                      '\n'
                                      'Legendary Actions\n'
                                      'Legendary Action Uses: 3. Immediately after another\n'
                                      'creature’s turn, the solar can expend a use to take one of\n'
                                      'the following actions. The solar regains all expended uses\n'
                                      'at the start of each of its turns.\n'
                                      'Blinding Gaze. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 25, one\n'
                                      'creature the solar can see within 120 feet. Failure: The\n'
                                      'target has the Blinded condition for 1 minute. Failure or\n'
                                      'Success: The solar can’t take this action again until the\n'
                                      'start of its next turn.\n'
                                      'Radiant Teleport. The solar teleports up to 60 feet to an\n'
                                      'unoccupied space it can see. Dexterity Saving Throw:\n'
                                      'DC 25, each creature in a 10-foot Emanation originat-\n'
                                      'ing from the solar at its destination space. Failure: 11\n'
                                      '(2d10) Radiant damage. Success: Half damage.\n'
                                      'Specter',
